  "lane": {
    "definition": "As scale_A protocol amendment 001 (three_point_rules, crc_obs of risk_upgrade amendment 004): a design with measured_only >= 3 is released with call active; any other design is released iff its exact margin > lambda; lambda is the first grid value with (sum_g L_g + 1)/(n_cal + 1) <= 1/10 for L_g(lambda) = (1/D_g) * sum over the group designs with measured_only < 3 of 1(margin > lambda) 1(call != truth); exact rational arithmetic.",
    "gate": "Every calibration and test design with measured_only >= 3 has truth active (0); otherwise the run stops.",
    "corruption": "The lane reads measured_only, which no rung corrupts. Corruption therefore reaches only the scores, calls and margins of designs outside the lane; lane designs are released as active on every rung.",
    "implementation": "Imported, not copied: summarize_headline.lane_lambdas and lane_rows define the lane at s = 0 and are compared row by row with the stress path. On every rung the stress path passes lane designs to run_start.single with call active; under the gate they carry zero loss, so the exact selection equals the lane rule with D_g over all designs of the group. Release = lane or (exact block > selected grid index). run_start.ExactRule margins are compared with the exact twin of release paper_nested_decision.apply_rule at s = 0.",
    "wells": "A lane design charges its measured wells, as the headline."
  },
  "ladder": "Unchanged from the parent protocol: noise levels, seeds, random streams, sigma definition (from each arm's own inner points), shrink, amplify and shuffle definitions.",
  "risk_calibration": "Unchanged alpha 1/10 and grid; lambda reselected per arm, rung, fold and seed on calibration identities with the lane.",
  "statistics": {
    "bootstrap": "4,000 identity-group resamples over the 188 sorted primary groups: the first draw of numpy default_rng(0), which equals the shared scale_A counts file bootstrap_identity_counts_seed0.npz (checked). One matrix for every readout, contrast and rung, so s = 0 reproduces the lane headline intervals. This replaces the parent choice of the nested draws for the same reason: the s = 0 row matches the intervals the manuscript prints.",
    "interval": "95% percentile interval, fixed decisions, no refitting uncertainty, no multiplicity correction.",
    "seeds": "As the parent protocol."
  },
  "readouts": {
